  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Nebraska totaled $1.2B in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 16,005 awards with an average award size of $77.7K. Obligations fell 1.7% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $406M, followed by the Department of Education with $293M and the General Services Administration with $218M. NELNET SERVICING LLC received the largest vendor total at $293M, while GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. followed with $201M. Other major industry categories include Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $293M and Computer Systems Design Services at $252M. Historical annual obligations show a peak at $2B in FY23 and mostly stable totals of $1.3B in FY21, FY22, FY24, and FY25. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date. This summary focuses on obligations and top buyers, vendors, and industries for contractors evaluating Nebraska’s federal market activity in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did federal spending in Nebraska change this year?",
        "body": "The state recorded $1.2B in obligations for FY2026 to date, down 1.7% year over year. Annual obligations peaked at $2B in FY23 and were $1.3B in FY21, FY22, FY24, and FY25. Current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. The award count is 16,005 and the average award size is $77.7K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors dominate federal awards in Nebraska?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense led buying with $406M, followed by the Department of Education at $293M and the General Services Administration at $218M. The largest vendor was NELNET SERVICING LLC at $293M, then GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $201M, and METGREEN SOLUTIONS INC at $121M. Other top industries were Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation at $293M and Computer Systems Design Services at $252M."
      }
    ]
